i was pleased to  hear the education secretary say  yesterday that  the government was supporting  face-to-face teaching in our  universities  come the autumn and the new new academic  turn but  that says to me that the government  should recognize that young people  haven't had that over the last year in  universities  and they spent over 9 000 pounds in  tuition fees for not having what they  should have which is face-to-face  learning  and i want to see the government  prioritizing young people and making  reparation to young people coming out of  this pandemic and i would say to them  they should give all young people who've  paid full tuition fees  the academic year 20 20 21 a 50  rebate on those fees because actually  this younger generation has given so  much i think  uh in terms of life chances and lost  opportunity through this pandemic  and i've not yet heard from the prime  minister or any minister  how they are going to help this younger  generation kind of repair the damage  get their lives back on track coming out  of this pandemic and i hope some mps on  the liaison committee  start to ask him some serious questions  about this  as well as questions about how he is  going to make  leveling up a real thing coming out of  this pandemic and not just a  scheme that benefits some favored places  rather than places that will really need  his support
 

